title op6: a split against a quiet side

# One of four shapes for the PENDING set-delta succession proposal
# (op6-set-succession.md).  The proposal is not adopted: the lead has
# not confirmed it, and nothing here authorizes implementing it.
#
# GOLD POLICY for the four op6 fixtures.  The gold section below
# records what the engine decides TODAY, so the suite stays a true
# regression gate while the proposal is pending.  Each fixture's
# comment states exactly what set-delta succession would change, in
# the form the new gold would take.  When the lead confirms, flipping
# a fixture is a one-line edit and the fixture becomes the proof that
# the change landed rather than a fixture that was always going to
# agree with whatever ran.
#
# This one is the control.  Onto un-shares z from the hard-linked
# triple; off-of does nothing at all.  There is no delta, so there is
# no succession question, and nothing in the proposal touches it.
#
# Today: clean, onto's split stands.
# Under the proposal: identical.  A control that changes would mean
# the proposal had reached further than it claims to.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      10-100: z

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      10-100: z

# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect clean

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0
